Given vectors $\overrightarrow {a} = (1, -3)$ and $\overrightarrow {b} = (-2, m)$, and $\overrightarrow {a}$ is perpendicular to ($\overrightarrow {a} - \overrightarrow {b}$).  
(1) Find the value of the real number $m$;  
(2) When $k\overrightarrow {a} + \overrightarrow {b}$ is parallel to $\overrightarrow {a} - \overrightarrow {b}$, find the value of the real number $k$.

Regular octagon $ABCDEFGH$ has its center at $J$.  Each of the vertices and the center are to be associated with one of the digits $1$ through $9$, with each digit used once, in such a way that the sums of the numbers on the lines $AJE$, $BJF$, $CJG$, and $DJH$ are all equal.  In how many ways can this be done?
