In $\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, $C$ are $a$, $b$, $c$ respectively. Given vectors $\overrightarrow{m}=(b,a-2c)$, $\overrightarrow{n}=(\cos A-2\cos C,\cos B)$, and $\overrightarrow{m} \perp \overrightarrow{n}$.
