Given an ellipse C: $\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \frac{y^2}{b^2} = 1$ ($a > b > 0$) with an eccentricity of $\frac{1}{2}$, and a circle centered at the origin with the radius equal to the semi-minor axis of the ellipse is tangent to the line $\sqrt{7}x - \sqrt{5}y + 12 = 0$.  
