Given the function $f(x) = f'(1)e^{x-1} - f(0)x + \frac{1}{2}x^2$ (where $f'(x)$ is the derivative of $f(x)$, and $e$ is the base of the natural logarithm), and $g(x) = \frac{1}{2}x^2 + ax + b$ ($a \in \mathbb{R}, b \in \mathbb{R}$):

