In the Cartesian coordinate system $xOy$, the parametric equation of line $l_{1}$ is $\begin{cases} x=t- \sqrt {3} \\ y=kt\end{cases}$ (where $t$ is the parameter), and the parametric equation of line $l_{2}$ is $\begin{cases} x= \sqrt {3}-m \\ y= \frac {m}{3k}\end{cases}$ (where $m$ is the parameter). Let $p$ be the intersection point of $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$. When $k$ varies, the trajectory of $p$ is curve $C_{1}$  
